Greg Harris created KAFKA-17103:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: MockClient tight loops when no metadata is present in=
 KafkaProducerTest
                 Key: KAFKA-17103
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17103
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Test
          Components: clients
            Reporter: Greg Harris


MockClient can throw this exception:
{noformat}
[2024-07-09 13:19:33,574] ERROR [Producer clientId=3Dproducer-1] Uncaught e=
rror in kafka producer I/O thread: =C2=A0(org.apache.kafka.clients.producer=
.internals.Sender:253)
java.lang.IllegalStateException: No previous metadata update to use
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.clients.MockClient$DefaultMockMetadataUpd=
ater.updateWithCurrentMetadata(MockClient.java:700)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.clients.MockClient.poll(MockClient.java:3=
23)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.internals.Sender.runOnce=
(Sender.java:349)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.clients.producer.internals.Sender.run(Sen=
der.java:251)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 at java.base/java.lang.Thread.run(Thread.java:829){noformat}
This happens whenever the MockClient.DefaultMockMetadataUpdater#lastUpdate =
variable is null, which is the case whenever there has not been any mock me=
tadata update.

In practice, this appears to happen in KafkaProducerTest#testTopicExpiryInM=
etadata, KafkaProducerTest#testTopicRefreshInMetadata, KafkaProducerTest#te=
stTopicNotExistingInMetadata. These three tests also use busy-waiting to ha=
ve another thread wait for the metadata update request and then provide the=
 metadata update.

We should find some mechanism to allow mocking these metadata updates that =
avoids this busy waiting/tight looping pattern, as it introduces an opportu=
nity for nondeterminism and wastes CPU cycles.

The solution should remove any usage of Thread.sleep/Utils.sleep/Time.SYSTE=
M.
Ideally the solution wouldn't require an additional test thread, but this i=
s optional.



