hi Michael

Thanks for sharing. I have read those two discussion threads.

The replicas assignment is a interesting topic to me, so the following
questions are used for my education (and learn something from this KIP)

Question: 1

When adding brokers to a cluster, Kafka currently does not always place new
> partitions on new brokers


I guess there are two ways to address that requirement:

1. (KIP-1066) update configs of all older brokers to make their folders get
cordoned. Also, they have to un-cordon the folders of all older brokers at
some point in time.
2. (current): manually define the assignments in creating topics. Or do
post-balance to move the assignments from older brokers to new brokers

It seems to me both ways require users to set something "manually". The
main difference is KIP-1066 can leverage server-side assignment policy,
right?

Question: 2

When removing brokers/log directories, there is no way to prevent Kafka
> from placing new replicas on these brokers/log directories


This is a good scenario. Especially, the new topics having a single replica
should not be hosted by the removing broker.

Question: 3

What happens if a preferred dir is marked as a cordoned folder? For
example:

scenario 1:
1. folder_a is marked as cordoned folder
2. users sent AlterReplicaLogDirs to create preferred folder_a for specific
partition

scenario 2:
1. users sent AlterReplicaLogDirs to create preferred folder_a for specific
partition
2. folder_a is marked as cordoned folder

Question: 4

Why does `BrokerRegistrationRequest` need to include `CordonedLogDirs` if
the broker will send `BrokerHeartbeatRequest` including `CordonedLogDirs`
later? It seems a little delay should be fine, as the final decision of
picking a folder is up to the broker.

Question: 5

So if a broker is offline, its cordoned log directories are still available
> to the controller when assigning partitions.


Pardon me, not sure why the controller should consider the folders of offli=
ne
brokers?

Thanks!
Chia-Ping


