Chia-Ping Tsai created KAFKA-17123:
--------------------------------------

             Summary: update docs of Storage Tool to clarify that "cluster id" can be non-uuid format after 3.7
                 Key: KAFKA-17123
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17123
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
            Reporter: Chia-Ping Tsai
            Assignee: Chia-Ping Tsai


see [https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/14628#discussion_r1674554451]

The uuid check is removed from 3.7, but we still generate the cluster id by "random-uuid". Hence, it would be nice to clarify that kafka don't require the cluster id must be uuid format



