> When a connector or task tries to read the offsets from the offsets topic=
, it issues `OffsetStorageImpl#offsets` method. This method gets a Future f=
rom the underneath KafkaBackingStore. KafkaBackingStore invokes `KafkaBased=
Log#readToEnd` method and passes the Callback. This method essentially adds=
 the Callback to a Queue of callbacks that are being managed.
> Within KafkaBasedLog, there's a WorkThread which keeps polling over the c=
allback queue and executes them and it does this in an infinite loop. Howev=
er, there is an enclosing try/catch block around the while loop. If there's=
 an exception thrown which is not caught by any of the other catch blocks, =
the control goes to the outermost catch block and the WorkThread is termina=
ted. However, the connectors/tasks are not aware of this and they would kee=
p submitting callbacks to KafkaBasedLog with nobody processing them. This c=
an be seen in the thread dumps as well:
