Greg Harris created KAFKA-17148:
-----------------------------------

             Summary: Kafka storage tool prints MetadataPropertiesEnsemble
                 Key: KAFKA-17148
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17148
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
            Reporter: Greg Harris


Using this following command on 3.6 branche yields this result:

=C2=A0
{noformat}
$ bin/kafka-storage.sh format --config config/kraft/server.properties --clu=
ster-id "$(bin/kafka-storage.sh random-uuid)"
Formatting /tmp/kraft-combined-logs with metadata.version 3.6-IV2.{noformat=
}
While on 3.7 it has this behavior:

=C2=A0
{noformat}
$ bin/kafka-storage.sh format --config config/kraft/server.properties --clu=
ster-id "$(bin/kafka-storage.sh random-uuid)"
SLF4J: Class path contains multiple SLF4J bindings.
...
SLF4J: Actual binding is of type [org.slf4j.impl.Reload4jLoggerFactory]
metaPropertiesEnsemble=3DMetaPropertiesEnsemble(metadataLogDir=3DOptional.e=
mpty, dirs=3D{/tmp/kraft-combined-logs: EMPTY})
Formatting /tmp/kraft-combined-logs with metadata.version 3.7-IV4.
{noformat}
and on 3.8:
{noformat}
$ bin/kafka-storage.sh format --config config/kraft/server.properties --clu=
ster-id "$(bin/kafka-storage.sh random-uuid)"
metaPropertiesEnsemble=3DMetaPropertiesEnsemble(metadataLogDir=3DOptional.e=
mpty, dirs=3D{/tmp/kraft-combined-logs: EMPTY})
Formatting /tmp/kraft-combined-logs with metadata.version 3.8-IV0.{noformat=
}
This doesn't appear to be a useful log message for users, so could be elimi=
nated.

=C2=A0

=C2=A0



