---------------------------------

             Summary: New consumer system tests pass for subset of tests, but fail if running all tests
                 Key: KAFKA-17183
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17183
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: clients, consumer, system tests
    Affects Versions: 3.8.0
            Reporter: Kirk True
            Assignee: Kirk True
             Fix For: 3.9.0


In 3.8, many of the system tests were updated to exercise both the old consumer and the new consumer. For quicker feedback, I have been creating a YAML-based test suite for just the subset of tests that were updated. When running the system tests in the subset, I am consistently seeing 100% pass rate. Recently I started running the entire test suite, and are now seeing many failures.

The cause is as yet unknown, but adding this here as a task to fix whatever is causing this behavior.



