Patrik M=C3=A1rton created KAFKA-17200:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: Enable MM2 to replicate topics ending in "internal" s=
uffix
                 Key: KAFKA-17200
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-17200
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: mirrormaker
            Reporter: Patrik M=C3=A1rton
            Assignee: Patrik M=C3=A1rton


In the current Mirror Maker 2 implementation, topics ending in ".internal" =
or "-internal" cannot be replicated as they are considered connect/mm2 inte=
rnal topics.=C2=A0

In some cases, users have business topics ending in ".internal" or "-intern=
al" that are excluded from the replication for the same reason. This is bec=
ause of two things:

(1) The ReplicationPolicy interface excludes all topics ending in ".interna=
l" or "-internal" from the replication, as they are considered internal con=
nect topics:
{code:java}
/** Internal topics are never replicated. */
default boolean isInternalTopic(String topic) {
    boolean isKafkaInternalTopic =3D topic.startsWith("__") || topic.starts=
With(".");
    boolean isDefaultConnectTopic =3D  topic.endsWith("-internal") ||  topi=
c.endsWith(".internal");
    return isMM2InternalTopic(topic) || isKafkaInternalTopic || isDefaultCo=
nnectTopic;
} {code}
(2) The DefaultTopicFilter has the following default exclude regular expres=
sion:
{code:java}
".*[\\-\\.]internal, .*\\.replica, __.*" {code}
The goal of this ticket is to enable the replication of such business topic=
s, while making sure that kafka internal topics are not replicated.

*Solution 1:* The DefaultTopicFilter can be configured to have a different =
exclude list with more specific regex to exclude all kafka internal topics,=
 but include business internal topics, eg.:
{code:java}
"mm2.*[\\-\\.]internal, .*\\.replica, __.*"; {code}
As these topics are explicitly excluded in the ReplicationPolicy interface =
too, we can have a new replication policy from DefaultReplicationPolicy, th=
at preserves the same behavior, but overrides the isInternalTopic() method =
in a way that topics ending with the internal suffix are not considered int=
ernal topics. Obviously in this case it would be important to set up the to=
pic filter correctly to avoid replicating kafka internal topics.

=C2=A0



