Subject: Re: [DISCUSS] KIP-971 Expose replication-offset-lag MirrorMaker2 metric
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi,

> My thinking is that any partition could go stale if there are no records
being produced into it.

1. Why would the value become stale if there are no new records? The
lag should stay the same, no?

> If enough of such partitions are present and are owned by a single MM tas=
k, an OOM could happen.

2. We already have a dozen of metrics per partition [0]. Why do you
think adding a few more would cause OutOfMemory errors?
Each task should only emit metrics for partitions it owns.

> Regarding the scenario where the TTL value is lower than the refresh inte=
rval - I believe that this is an edge that we need to document and prevent =
against, for example either failing to start on such a combination or resor=
ting to a default value that would satisfy the constraint and logging an er=
ror.

3. Can you add the behavior you propose in the KIP?

Thanks,
Mickael

0: https://github.com/apache/kafka/blob/trunk/connect/mirror/src/main/java/=
org/apache/kafka/connect/mirror/MirrorSourceMetrics.java#L71-L106

